	<td width="100%" align="left" valign="top">
		<p><font size="5">The Polished Granite Tomahawk (heritage quest)<br /></font><p>Results in Guild XP, Status Points, and this Dual wield weapon: <a href="http://eq2.ogaming.com/db/items/PolishedGraniteTomahawk.php" target="_blank"><u><font color="#0000ff" size="2">http://eq2.ogaming.com/db/items/PolishedGraniteTomahawk.php</font></u></a></p><ol><font size="2"></font><li>Learn the Giant language. You must inspect 6 Hill Giant Idols. They are a chest drop only. You can buy them from other players for between 1G and 10G a piece. The most I paid was 3G. Check the broker as well.<br /></li><li>Speak to Osid BoulderBoom. He is located in the midst of the highest level giants in TS. On the same plateau as &quot;The Banished&quot; You must speak giant to get the quest. He is an attackable mob, so PCs kill him thinking he&#39;s named and has loot. He HAS NO LOOT. So you may end up waiting. I waited for nearly 2 hours once. This is a problem almost every time you need to talk to him. Remember to check both TS instances. (TS1 and TS2)<br /></li><li>You must rescue &quot;Tarby BoulderBoom&quot; Osids lost bear. He is located at +508.45, -1.18, +483.55 in TS. Near Point #14 on this map: <a href="http://www.gry-online.pl/eq2/maps.asp?ID=52" target="_blank"><u><font color="#0000ff" size="2">http://www.gry-online.pl/eq2/maps.asp?ID=52</font></u></a><font size="2"> Here is a Link to the &quot;Little Lost Tarby&quot; quest: </font><a href="http://eq2.ogaming.com/db/quests/LittleTarbyLost.php" target="_blank"><u><font color="#0000ff" size="2">http://eq2.ogaming.com/db/quests/LittleTarbyLost.php</font></u></a><font size="2"> He is not Always up, but he is common spawn. No place holder. Remember to Check both TS instances. After you hail him you must kill 3 waves of Level 25+ wolves that get progressively more difficult. Hail Tarby again and you can pick him up.<br /></font></li><li>Return to Osid BolderBoom to receive the heritage quest &quot;An Axe from the Past&quot; Found here: <a href="http://eq2.ogaming.com/db/quests/AnAxefromThePast.php" target="_blank"><u><font color="#0000ff" size="2">http://eq2.ogaming.com/db/quests/AnAxefromThePast.php</font></u></a><font size="2"> He will also give you a cracked axe to repair.<br /></font></li><li>Now you must mine 10 Pristine granite pieces from the &quot;Wind swept rocks&quot; in TS. You must have 90+ mining to do so and Wind Swept Rocks are a little more rare than you think so this can take a while.<br /></li><li>After collecting all the Granite pieces you will automatically receive a recipe and a few components. You are only missing &quot;Coal&quot; (about 60c on the vendor in the tradeskill instance) and &quot;A Fir Stave&quot; Unfortunately, a Fir stave requires &quot;Severed Fir&quot; to create and 20+ Woodworking. &quot;Severed Fir&quot; is a Tier 3 rare which means it sells for around 10g. Plus you need to hire a woodworker (that wont steal your 10g item) to make you the fir stave. Check the Broker for the fir. The woodworks will rarely have extra.<br /></li><li>Once you have the Fir Stave, the coal and the quest components, it&#39;s time to combine. YOU have to do this part because the quest items are No-Trade. I&#39;ve heard that you need to be at least level 10 to combine, but I&#39;m not sure if I believe that. I was able to do it (I&#39;m level 14 alchemist) and there was no hint of a problem. You must do the combine at a forge.<br /></li><li>You will now have&nbsp;an Axe.&nbsp;This Axe has poor stats and was red to me at level 30. Basically worthless. But you take the Axe Back to Osid and he tells you to sharpen it on the &quot;Wandering Dead&quot; (100 Skeletons in TS) You&#39;d think the easiest would be the grays near the docks... but they aren&#39;t. The best place is the &quot;Solo&quot; skeletons near ROV. With a level 27 Paladin that was nearby and bored I did this part in 45 minutes.<br /></li><li>You will now have a 2nd Axe! (no, the first doesn&#39;t poof) This axe is much better: <a href="http://eq2.ogaming.com/db/items/SharpenedGraniteTomahawk.php" target="_blank"><font color="#e69f4d">http://eq2.ogaming.com/db/items/SharpenedGraniteTomahawk.php</font></a><br />It is better than&nbsp;most player made items of equivalent level.<br /></li><li>Talk to Osid again, this time he is not sure if he can trust you. Apparently slaughtering half the zone for him wasn&#39;t quite enough. So he wants you to prove yourself by killing 25 Skindancer Gnolls in under 1 hour. I had a level 35 help me with this part so it was easy. They were green to me at 30.<br /></li><li>Talk to Osid BolderBoom again and he gives you the Final part of the Quest: Kill The Octogorgon Which is located in The HIGH LEVEL version of The Cove of Decay. Currently the Octogorgon is Bugged. Supposedly he casts an AOE Lifetap that hits NPCs as well as PCs. So when he casts it the encounter becomes broken and you can not get quest credit. This is what happened to me and why I couldn&#39;t finish the quest. Supposedly if you cast a &quot;Stifle&quot; or &quot;Silence&quot; type spell on him it will prevent this and allow you to finish the quest. I can confirm that he is bugged but I have tried this fix with no success.</li></ol></p>
