	<td width="100%" align="left" valign="top">
		This is a heritage quest that results in Dwarven Work Boots. It is given by Hwal Rucksif in Antonica (-559, -12, -316). <br /><br />Step 1 is to harvest 100 Ore and 100 Wood from Antonica. It must be in Antonica and the get around of passing items back and forth will not work. <br /><br />After completing the harvest you must return to Hwal with at least 50 Ore and Wood in your inventory. However he doesn&#39;t take them from inventory. You are rewarded with some coin (approx 11s) and the next step. <br /><br />Next requires you to collect three more pieces for Hwal: <br /><br />The first is from the Blackburrow. It drops from miners and excavaters. <br /><br />The second is from a named Sapling in Stormold, near library entrance. Clear the fungus and mist to spawn him. <br /><br />The third piece from drop Bloodtalon, a named Griffon in the Thundering Steppes. <br /><br />Hwal then tells you that all this forging is making him thursty. He sends you to Blackburrow to get some stout. It&#39;s in the Brewery, the top barrel on a a stack of barrels just as you get in (need loc). <br /><br />After you go back to Hwal he tells you about a family curse. Get a group and go out to Vhalen Tower (-1300, +38, +45) in Antonica. Hwal&#39;s grandfather is in a instanced dungeon that you get into by clicking the a piece of rubble on the floor. <br /><br />Kill his grandfather and reutrn to Hwal. He then sends you to get pieces for his new boots. You need to collect the following items from the Thundering Steppes: <br /><br />- Leather from a Mature Antelope <br />- Ore from a Firerock Scout <br /><br />Give these items to Minty Frostbeard at Thundermist Vilalge in the Thundering Steppes. She will tell you she needs time and to come back in 72 minutes. So go do something else for that time and then come back. She will give you the boots for Hwal. <br /><br />Take the boots to Hwal in Antonica and he will give you his old boots for your efforts. Congratulations on Dwarven Work Boots.
