	<td width="14" style="background-image:url(/skins/north_qeynos2_1/images/box/left.gif); background-repeat:repeat-y;"><img src="/skins/north_qeynos2_1/images/box/left.gif" width="14" height="100%"></td>
	<td width="100%" align="left" valign="top">
		<div><font color="#ffffff"><u><font face="Times New Roman" size="5">GHOULBANE WALKTHROUGH</font></u> </font></div><p><font size="3"><font face="Times New Roman"><font color="#ffffff"><span>&nbsp;</span>I got tired of looking at 20 different post on the EQ2 forums trying to find information on the Ghoulbane quest and have decided to try and put it all together in one spot for easy reference. Let me start off by saying this is a work in progress and will be updated when new information is found and confirmed to be true.</font></font></font></p><p><font size="3"><font face="Times New Roman"><font color="#ffffff"><span>&nbsp;</span>At this time no one has completed the entire quest so there are still several questions about the quest and the actual sword. One being if the Ghoulbane will be a Paladin only weapon or be equipable by anyone that can use swords. I am of the belief that it will be equipable by any class and so plan on including a guide for how evil races/classes can obtain the quest in this guide also.</font></font></font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff" size="3"></font>&nbsp;</p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3"><font color="#ffffff">If you are having any trouble findin a paticular npc or area mentioned in this guide most can be found in these maps. </font><a href="http://www.gry-online.pl/eq2/index.asp" target="_blank"><font color="#ffffff">http://www.gry-online.pl/eq2/index.asp</font></a></font></p><p><font size="3"><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff"></font></font>&nbsp;</p><div><font color="#ffffff"><u><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">The Dusty Blue Stone</font></u> </font></div><p><u><font size="3"><font face="Times New Roman"></font></font></u>&nbsp;</p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffff00" size="3">To start the quest you will need to speak to Vida Sweeps in Nettleville Hovel. Vida has worn out her broom and needs you to run and get her a new one from Tawli Whiskwind in Baubleshire. When you bring the broom back to Vida she will give you the Dusty Blue Stone. Examine the stone to get the next part of the quest. The stone is tradable but can only be examined once for the quest.</font></p><p><font size="3"><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff"></font></font>&nbsp;</p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff" size="3">(I will get the exact text when I can. If anyone already has it please send it to me so I can include it in the guide)</font></p><p><font size="3"><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff"></font></font>&nbsp;</p><p><font size="3"><font face="Times New Roman"><font color="#ffffff"><b>Evil Side ¿ </b>The best way for someone from Freeport to start this is just to make another character on the Qeynos side. Run through the Isle of Refuge, get to Qeynos and then talk to Vida Sweeps. All of the quest takes place inside the city and just requires you to run around. After you get the stone (Don¿t examine it) just hand it to someone you trust and then switch to your Freeport character to get the stone back and continue on to the next part of the quest.</font></font></font></p><p><font size="3"><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff"></font></font>&nbsp;</p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffff00" size="3">After examing the stone it will tell you to seek out a Gemstone expert. It is referring to Gruffin Goldtooth in Graystone Yard. Once you speak with Gruffin he will tell you he needs 40 rock samples from the Thundering Steppes. He asks you to collect these while he studies the stone. </font></p><p><b><font size="3"><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff"></font></font></b>&nbsp;</p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff" size="3">(Again I will get the exact text for this when I can. If anyone already has it please send it to me so I can include it in the guide)</font></p><p><font size="3"><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff"></font></font>&nbsp;</p><p><font size="3"><font face="Times New Roman"><font color="#ffffff"><b>Evil Side ¿ </b>In order for a Freeport citizen to complete this part of the quest they will need to sneak in to Qeynos. The best way to do this is to enter The Peat Bog from Antonica. Once in Peat Bog head to Vermin¿s Syne. Once in Vermin¿s Syne you will be right next to the zone in to The Down Below. Once in The Down Below make your way to Graystone Yard. You will come out in Graystone near Gruffin. The only problem is there is one guard that stands near the miners. If you haven¿t experienced the fun of sneaking in to the opposing city yet you may or may not know that the guards wont kill you but they will throw you out if they see you. The best plan at this point is to bring along another Freeport friend with you and have then agro the guard. While the guard is chasing down your friend you can take the opportunity to run up to Gruffin and get this part of the quest. It may take you a few times to get the timing on this down but it is doable. </font></font></font></p><p><font size="3"><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff"></font></font>&nbsp;</p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff" size="3"><font color="#ffff00">Once you have gotten your quest updated its time to start collecting the rock samples for Gruffin. To harvest materials in Thundering Steppes you need to get your mining skill to 91. If you haven¿t been working on mining lately it might be a good time to grab the ¿These Boots Where Made For Walking¿ heritage quest from Hwal Rucksif at Ardent Needle Keep in Antonica.<span>&nbsp; </span>The first part of this quest involves collecting 100 ore and 100 elms. While you are in Antonica working on your mining skill might as well get credit for the boots quest. This is what I did and by the time I harvested 100 ore my mining skill had risen to 93</font>. </font></p><p><font size="3"><font face="Times New Roman"><font color="#ffffff">Regardless once you get your mining skill high enough to start collecting in Thundering Steppes head that way and get it done. The rock samples you need only drop from Wind Swept Stones. I wish I could tell you a specific area to mine in but I wasn¿t able to locate any area that seemed better than another. Though in the field near the giants camp</font></font></font><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff" size="3">Wind Swept Stones seemed to appear on a more regular basis.</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff" size="3">Once you have the samples you will need to head back to Gruffin Goldtooth in Graystone Yard. Upon hailing Gruffin he will say</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;Hail there! Were you able to get the stone samples yet?&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;Yes I have them right here.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;Perfect! These will help greatly in finding new places to mine. Qeynos is going to need strong buildings and walls to accomondate all the new people arriving.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;What did you find out about the blue stone?&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;I looked through all my books and I couldn&#39;t find one entry that matched its desciption, I even asked all my mining buddies out at the tavern and none of them knew what it is either, The strange thing is you can&#39;t even scratch it with Bopper&#39;s diamond paint pick!&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;So what should I do with it?&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;My advice is to take it to a mage. My hunch is this may be an enchanted stone of some kind. My only conclusion I can draw is that your stone isn&#39;t naturally from any parts we know of. I&#39;m sorry I couldn&#39;t tell you more. Good luck on your search!&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;Thanks for the help, Gruffin.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">When done with this you will recieve some coin and experience.</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffff00" size="3">The mage he is speaking of is Aristride Calais at the mage tower in South Qeynos. Upon hailing him </font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;Hello adventurer. Please mind the books and pages spread about. I am in the middle of researching ,ethods of enchanting stones with magical properties and it wouldn&#39;t do to have foot prints and smudges on the documents.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;Would you mind looking over a stone of mine? Gruffin Goldtooth thinks it could be enchanted.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;Gruffin says that? That dwarf really knows his minerals. I suppose I could take a look. Hmm... No, it can&#39;t be that. maybe it&#39;s a piece of rubicite... no no no. It might be a... hmmm.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;What is it?&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;Intriguing... I can&#39;t say what it is off hand. Id like to perform a few tests on it. Would you be willing to leave the stone with me for a short time? These tests could be dangerous if this turns out to be a cursed stone or something of that type. I wouldn&#39;t want to endanger anyone else.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;I can leave the stone with you.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;Thankyou. While I am testing this, would you mind running an errand for me? Olden Highguard, in Thundering Village, asked me to enchant a few bars of Ironforge Steel for him. I have them ready but I havn&#39;t had time to deliver them.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;I can do that.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;Excellent, I&#39;ll have some coin for you when you come back. I should also know something of this stone as well.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;I&#39;ll return soon.&quot;</font></p><p><font size="3"><font face="Times New Roman"><font color="#ffffff"><b>Evil Side </b>¿ In order to reach South Qeynos you will need to venture back down in to The Down Below and find the exit to South Qeynos. From this point you will just have to duck and cover until you figure out the guards patterns and make it to the tower. To make it to South Qeynos you will just need to head back to The Down Below and exit to South Qeynos from there. </font></font></font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffff00" size="3">Olden Highgaurd is in Thundering Village in the Thundering Steppes. Hail him and he will say </font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;Heather and I just made the journey from the docks. The trip went smoothly, although we felt like there were eyes upon us from high atop the rocks.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;I have some enchanted steel bars from Airstider.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;Ah, excellent. Thankyou very much for bringing them out to me. It can be a long journey from Qeynos out to this village. Iv&#39;e been wanting to work with enchanted steel for a long time now. Thanks again for bringing this by!&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffff00" size="3">Once you have spoken with Olden head back to South Qeynos and speak with Aristide once again.</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;Ah, there you are, did Olden get the enchanted steel bars I sent him?&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;Yes, he was happy to get them.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;Good, good. I performed my tests on your stone. It seems to have contained power of some kind, but the power was divine, not arcane. This stone was blessed, not enchanted. Unfortunantly, I know little about blessed objects. Maybe you could find someone here in Qeynos that would have a better understanding of these objects.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;Thankyou, Aristide&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">You will recieve some coin and experience</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffff00" size="3">You need to speak to Toranim Skyblade standing next to the Temple of Life in North Qeynos.</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;Greetings, adventurer. It is good to see citizens visiting the Temple of Life. Many great blessings can come from following the doctorins that one is taught here.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;I believe I might have a blessed stone. Would you mind taking a look at it?&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;Hmm... I do sense a holy energy radiating from it but it is very minor... as if it hasn&#39;t been used in a very long time. Yes, it still carries its blessing but it is faint. I know what this could be but my theory will need to be tested. Are you willing to try something for me?&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;What do you want me to do?&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;Take this stone and travel deep into the recently discovered home of the Knights of Thunder, Stormhold. There you will find dangerous creatures known as ghouls. Slay a number of the more powerful ones then return to me with the stone. This will be dangerous but I have faith you can do this.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;I&#39;ll slay the ghouls.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffff00" size="3">You now need to head to Stronghold and kill any undead. I killed the Defiled Sentries at the entrance, who were grey to me, and still recived quest credit. Once you have killed 28 undead head back to North Qeynos and speak to Toranim again.</font><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffff00" size="3">At this point when you talk to Toranim you will be done with the Dusty Blue Stone. If you are a class that wouldn¿t be able use a sword you can choose to end the quest at this point. If you end it now you will get some decent experience and a choice between a couple of different items that might suit your particular class. If you choose to continue the quest you will receive the Restoring Ghoulbane heritage quest.</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;Hello, adventurer. Were you able to defeat the ghouls in Stormhold?&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;Yes, the stone feels warmer and is faintly glowing now.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;I knew it would be. What you hold in your hand is the blessed adornment that once rested within the holy blade, Ghoulbane. It was consecrated by the priests of Life to assist paladins of good in the destruction of the undead.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;If I have the adornment, where is the sword?&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;As the tale goes, the Ghoulbane was passed down through generations until it found it&#39;s way into the hands of a honerable Knight of Thunder. This paladin was well known for seeking out evil corruption of the undead where ever it could be found. The legend claims the paladin carried Ghoulbane one last time on a crusade the paladin would never finish.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;What happened to him?&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;He would never return from that journey. His squire returned sometime later here in Qeynos telling of the hordes of undead that poured out of the castle as his brave lord fought valiantly to vanquish the darkness but they were to much... Ghoulbane had failed him and the squire had fled.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;So Ghoulbane rest in that castle?&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;No the Knights of Thunder mounted an attack on the castle when the word had reached them that the paladin had fallen. They did find the spot where the paladin was slain. All that was recovered was the sword. Strangrly, it was reported that the adornment was missing.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;So the knights have the sword?&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;Yes, they placed it within the tomb of the Stormlords in rememberance of the fallen paladin. The sword should be still in the tomb. If you could gain access to it, you could retrieve the Ghoulebane. Bring it here to me and I will be able to perform the ritual to reseal the adornment to the sword.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;That sounds like a plan. I&#39;ll work on recovering the sword.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;Very good. Seek out the sword in the tomb of the Stormlords within Stormhold. Bring it to me and I will combine the sword with it&#39;s adornment.&quot;</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&quot;I hope to be back soon.&quot;</font></p><p><font color="#ffff00">(This is as far as I have gotten in the quest myself. Anything from this point on will be information from various post and websites until I can confirm for myself)</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff" size="3"></font></p><p><font size="3"><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff"></font></font>&nbsp;</p><div><font color="#ffffff"><u><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">Restoring Ghoulbane</font></u> </font></div><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff" size="3">Information gets a little sketchy here but it seems that Toranim task you with going back to Stormhold and killing Storm Lords and collecting a sword. Apparently to get the sword you need access to the Tomb of Valor.</font></p><p><font size="3"><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff"></font></font>&nbsp;</p><p><u><font size="3"><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff">A Key To The Past (ToV Access)</font></font></u></p><p><u><font size="3"><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff"></font></font></u>&nbsp;</p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff" size="3">This quest starts with a Crushed Librarian, oddly enough he hangs out in the Library in Stormhold. Depending on your level you may want to bring a group with you to get to the Crushed Librarian. There are some pretty tough mobs in the area around him.</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff" size="3">The first part of this quest involves finding three missing journal pages. If I remember correctly the pages can be found on Defiled Squires (It has been awhile since I did this part. After getting all three pages return to the Crushed Librarian and he will send you on the next step of the quest.</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff" size="3">The next part of this quest involves finding a couple more journal pages from two named mobs and some handmaidens. The first named, Lord Andros can be found near the chessboard on the first level. The next named, Guard Captain Hess is near the barracks before you get to the spiral staircase with the glowing sword. The last mob you need to kill are the Handmaidens in level two just past the Atrium. Once you have defeated all three return to the Librarian and he will tell you that you need to find a key.</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff" size="3">The key is located by Sir Valinayle near the entrance to Stormhold. In the cubby to the right of him you can see the key lying on the ground. You cannot pick it up until you have finished the other parts of the quest. Once you have picked the key you are ready to go enter the Tomb of Valor.</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff" size="3">A couple of things to note about the Tomb of Valor. </font></p><p><font size="3"><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff"></font></font>&nbsp;</p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff" size="3">I have heard that there is a slight delay, 5 or 6 minutes, each time someone loots the key from next to Sir Valinayle.</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff" size="3">ToV is an instanced zone that has time restrictions for how often you can access it.</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff" size="3">You must have a group of at least three people who have all completed the ToV access quest in order to enter ToV.</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff" size="3">Now back to the Ghoulbane quest</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffff00" size="3">Once you have your group and get in to ToV you have couple of choices. Apparently ToV is a large room with several coffins. By clicking on the coffins some type of ring event is started that eventually spawns the Storm Lord. Your first choice is to get a good group and defeat the ring event and Storm Lord then loot the sword off of the wall.</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffff00" size="3">Your second choice is apparently to zone in. Not to touch the coffins or agro any mobs and to simply walk over to the wall and loot the sword and leave. </font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff" size="3">(Several people have reported that only one sword may be looted for each instance of ToV. So if more than one person needs the sword, 1 person will get it and the next will have to wait until they are able to enter the instanced zone again. </font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff" size="3">After retrieving the sword you will need to go speak with Toranim Skyblade again at the Temple of Life. At this point you will receive the Weakened Ghoulbane.</font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff" size="3">There is more to the quest to restore the Ghoulbane to its full power but right now it is still pretty sketchy. I will continue to update this guide as I get further in to the quest myself. </font></p><p><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff" size="3">I would ask anyone that has more specific information about the parts of the quest I have already covered or the quest after this point or any mistakes that might be noticed to please post here or e-mail me at </font><a href="mailto:LemJe@Bellsouth.net" target="_blank"><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff" size="3">LemJe@Bellsouth.net</font></a><font face="Times New Roman" color="#ffffff" size="3"> so I can continue to improve this walkthrough. </font></p><div><font color="#ffffff"><span>I would like to thank all the people who have posted on the EQ2 boards and across the web for forging the way on this quest. I in no way claim any of the information in this guide as my own. I have only collected it all and put in one area.</span><br /><br /></font></div><div><font color="#ffffff">12-16-04&nbsp; Updated the dialogue with Grubbin Goldtooth, Aristide Calais and Toranim Skyblade. Also achnged first part of quest that stated if you are a Freeport citizen you need to make an alt in Qeynos and finish the citizen quest. Since the quest only involves going to the various villages, citizenship is not needed.(Thanks for pointing that out Carancir)</font></div>
		<p>
